Apple today seeded the release candidate of an upcoming iOS 27.2 update to developers for testing purposes, with the update coming a week after Apple released the fourth iOS 27.2 beta. Apple also seeded the iPadOS 27.2 RC.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
Registered developers can download the beta updates by opting in under Settings > General > Software Update and selecting the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> developer beta.<br/>
<br/>
The beta was used to test the new &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; Health app, but the features have since been removed and will be coming in a later update. It expands <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI to new languages including French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish.<br/>
<br/>
There are now profiles for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app, Call Context supports anniversary alerts, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> has a new icon. The update also supports an alternative expanded prompt for App Tracking Transparency in the European Union.<br/>
<br/>
